; examples/s0-heartbeat/system-non-harmonic.eadl — the discrimination case.
;
; ⛔ THIS FILE EXISTS BECAUSE THE THREE F28 CASES SHARE A BLIND SPOT. Their periods are 10 and 30,
; then 10 and 20: in both, one period divides the other, so the task sets are **harmonic** and
; the hyperperiod equals the longest period. A realization that returned `max` instead of `lcm`
; therefore passes F28 end to end — found by mutating `lcm` to `max` in `crates/archogen-s0` and
; watching all twelve oracle tests stay green.
;
; Here `chime` is released every 15 ms against `beat`'s 10 ms. Nothing divides anything:
;
;   hyperperiod  lcm(10, 15) = 30 ms        longest period  15 ms
;   releases     beat at 0, 10, 20; chime at 0, 15 — five, interleaved
;
; ⭐ IT HAS NO FROZEN EXPECTATION, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. The three F28 cases were frozen before
; any emitter existed, which is what makes §12 S0's independence claim a fact of the commit
; order. This case was written afterwards, by leaf `S0.4`, so a frozen file beside it would carry
; a weaker pedigree than its neighbours and nobody reading the directory later would be able to
; tell which was which. Instead the oracle **derives** its expected observation from this
; description through its own implementation of the observation contract, and compares that to
; what the generated system prints — two independent implementations agreeing, rather than one
; implementation agreeing with itself.
;
; See examples/s0-heartbeat/README.md, "What the corpus cannot see".

(defblock console.uart
  (offers (observable-output true)))

(defplatform host.playground
  (offers (core-count 1 tick))
  (requires (uses console.uart)))

(defservice console.write
  (requires (needs observable-output)))

(defsystem heartbeat
  (task beat
    (period 10 ms) (deadline 10 ms) (deadline-from release)
    (priority 1) (uses console.write) (on-overrun fault))
  (task chime
    (period 15 ms) (deadline 15 ms) (deadline-from release)
    (priority 2) (uses console.write) (on-overrun fault))
  (requires (uses console.write))
  (platform (uses host.playground)))
